  "explanation": "The four listed resources are soil, air, water, and sunlight. For any form of life to exist on the Moon or another planet, the only universally required resources among these are water (as a solvent and for biochemical reactions) and an energy source (sunlight or another form of radiation). Soil is not required because life can grow in hydroponic or other non‑soil media, and \"air\" (Earth's mixture of oxygen and nitrogen) is not essential; life could use other gases or none at all. Therefore, only two of the four resources are strictly necessary.",
